1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,400
An AI wrote this line. Why? Nobody can answer that today.

2
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:22,800
agit writes every agent step into a git ledger: one step, one
commit.

3
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:41,050
The agent writes a failing test first, then the fix — and each
step is a commit.

4
00:00:41,050 --> 00:00:53,850
VERIFIED is not the model's opinion — agit ran your tests
before believing it.

5
00:00:53,850 --> 00:01:04,650
Human lines and agent lines, separated line by line.

6
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:18,650
Point at any line and ask why. The answer was stored when the
line was written.

7
00:01:18,650 --> 00:01:30,650
Rewind to step 4 and try a different approach. The ledger
branches like git.

8
00:01:30,650 --> 00:01:40,650
Two verified solutions to the same task, side by side.

9
00:01:40,650 --> 00:01:50,650
Diff the outcomes, then keep the one you prefer.

10
00:01:50,650 --> 00:02:04,250
Every model call is recorded, so a run replays
byte-identically — for free.

11
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:19,050
The dashboard: every run, every step, every reason — one
static HTML file.

12
00:02:19,050 --> 00:02:33,450
Click any line: the step and the reasoning pin to the top.

13
00:02:33,450 --> 00:02:42,450
And where the tokens actually went, step by step.

14
00:02:42,450 --> 00:02:54,050
Zero dependencies, 97 offline tests, and a demo that needs no
API key.

